WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.048
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Writing Skills.

2
00:00:05.348 --> 00:00:08.804
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.104 --> 00:00:15.263
Unit four: Describing People and Places. Today you will write a clear description with adjectives.

4
00:00:15.563 --> 00:00:18.331
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:22.291
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:24.151
Describe.

7
00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.568
Describe means to say what something is like.

8
00:00:28.183 --> 00:00:29.521
Describe your town.

9
00:00:30.117 --> 00:00:32.873
Your turn. Say: Describe.

10
00:00:35.733 --> 00:00:36.688
Describe.

11
00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:38.451
Adjective.

12
00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:42.193
Adjective means a word that describes a noun.

13
00:00:42.783 --> 00:00:44.446
Use a strong adjective.

14
00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:47.389
Your turn. Say: Adjective.

15
00:00:50.233 --> 00:00:51.269
Adjective.

16
00:00:52.017 --> 00:00:53.157
Appearance.

17
00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:56.463
Appearance means how a person looks.

18
00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:58.585
Describe her appearance.

19
00:00:59.183 --> 00:01:01.743
Your turn. Say: Appearance.

20
00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:05.787
Appearance.

21
00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:07.714
Personality.

22
00:01:08.717 --> 00:01:11.436
Personality means the way a person behaves.

23
00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:13.887
He has a kind personality.

24
00:01:14.483 --> 00:01:17.147
Your turn. Say: Personality.

25
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.129
Personality.

26
00:01:21.883 --> 00:01:23.105
Atmosphere.

27
00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:26.406
Atmosphere means the feeling of a place.

28
00:01:27.017 --> 00:01:29.132
The market has a lively atmosphere.

29
00:01:29.717 --> 00:01:32.404
Your turn. Say: Atmosphere.

30
00:01:35.267 --> 00:01:36.337
Atmosphere.

31
00:01:37.083 --> 00:01:37.841
Vivid.

32
00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:41.244
Vivid means clear and strong in the mind.

33
00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:43.443
Write a vivid description.

34
00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:46.215
Your turn. Say: Vivid.

35
00:01:49.067 --> 00:01:49.778
Vivid.

36
00:01:50.517 --> 00:01:51.704
Surroundings.

37
00:01:52.717 --> 00:01:55.320
Surroundings means the things around a place.

38
00:01:55.917 --> 00:01:57.533
The surroundings are quiet.

39
00:01:58.117 --> 00:02:00.827
Your turn. Say: Surroundings.

40
00:02:03.667 --> 00:02:05.062
Surroundings.

41
00:02:05.817 --> 00:02:06.609
Charming.

42
00:02:07.617 --> 00:02:09.825
Charming means pleasant and attractive.

43
00:02:10.417 --> 00:02:11.940
It is a charming village.

44
00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:15.028
Your turn. Say: Charming.

45
00:02:17.867 --> 00:02:18.705
Charming.

46
00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:23.685
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:27.362
Visal, how can I describe my hometown?

48
00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:37.212
Use clear adjectives and specific details. Say what you can see, hear and feel. Write about the surroundings and the atmosphere.

49
00:02:38.317 --> 00:02:40.049
And for describing a person?

50
00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:49.967
Write about appearance first, then personality. For example, she is tall and friendly, and she is always ready to help.

51
00:02:51.083 --> 00:02:53.153
Any tip for better adjectives?

52
00:02:54.250 --> 00:03:02.301
Avoid very common words like nice and good. Choose specific words like peaceful, charming or lively.

53
00:03:03.467 --> 00:03:05.095
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:08.890
Grammar focus: Adjective before a noun.

55
00:03:09.190 --> 00:03:10.458
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:12.604
a charming village

57
00:03:13.517 --> 00:03:14.924
the lively market

58
00:03:15.867 --> 00:03:21.259
Put the adjective before the noun and after be. Choose specific adjectives instead of nice or good.

59
00:03:22.017 --> 00:03:25.354
Be careful! Don't say: It is a village charming.

60
00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:29.416
Say: It is a charming village.

61
00:03:29.716 --> 00:03:31.274
Adjective before noun.

62
00:03:32.067 --> 00:03:34.928
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:35.733 --> 00:03:36.874
My Hometown.

64
00:03:37.174 --> 00:03:39.789
Sophea describes her hometown in Kampot.

65
00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:43.276
It is a charming town beside a quiet river.

66
00:03:44.267 --> 00:03:46.800
The market has a lively atmosphere in the morning.

67
00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:49.869
Her neighbours are friendly and helpful.

68
00:03:50.867 --> 00:03:53.830
She writes vivid details so readers can imagine it.

69
00:03:54.933 --> 00:03:58.854
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:03:59.717 --> 00:04:02.018
An adjective describes a blank.

71
00:04:02.318 --> 00:04:05.565
A, page. B, noun. C, verb.

72
00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:10.960
The answer is B: noun.

73
00:04:12.117 --> 00:04:14.372
Atmosphere means the blank of a place.

74
00:04:14.672 --> 00:04:18.000
A, price. B, size. C, feeling.

75
00:04:21.533 --> 00:04:23.347
The answer is C: feeling.

76
00:04:24.483 --> 00:04:26.355
Vivid means clear and blank.

77
00:04:26.655 --> 00:04:29.728
A, strong. B, small. C, late.

78
00:04:33.267 --> 00:04:34.941
The answer is A: strong.

79
00:04:36.083 --> 00:04:38.396
Avoid very common words like blank.

80
00:04:38.696 --> 00:04:41.874
A, market. B, nice. C, river.

81
00:04:45.433 --> 00:04:47.119
The answer is B: nice.

82
00:04:48.283 --> 00:04:50.225
Sophea's hometown is in blank.

83
00:04:50.525 --> 00:04:54.271
A, Paris. B, Tokyo. C, Kampot.

84
00:04:57.833 --> 00:04:59.821
The answer is C: Kampot.

85
00:05:01.033 --> 00:05:04.626
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:05.483 --> 00:05:07.413
How do you describe a place?

87
00:05:16.217 --> 00:05:17.671
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:17.971 --> 00:05:31.202
I use specific adjectives and write what I can see, hear and feel. I describe the surroundings and the atmosphere. I avoid common words like nice and choose vivid words.

89
00:05:31.502 --> 00:05:33.780
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:34.683 --> 00:05:38.799
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and adjective before a noun.

91
00:05:39.099 --> 00:05:43.365
Today's value is imagination. Imagine new ideas for a better future.

92
00:05:43.665 --> 00:05:46.015
See you in Unit five. Goodbye!

93
00:05:46.315 --> 00:05:48.933
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

